In message <cs1kn5$n1t$1@online.de>, Janis Papanagnou wrote:
..
> I hope to understand your text correctly and you mean that _recover_ is
> "unnecessary" in case that you just stopped the process.

Absolutely; running recover on a set of game files currently being used by a
running process will (the next time the game needs to look at the files) cause
death by trickery.

As long as we're having a debate over process control syntax, by the way, the
original poster could (probably; as with any other process syntax including the
"fg" command this depends on what shell you're running) merely have typed
"%nethack" to bring the game process forward again.

Actually, since he probably didn't have any other processes whose names start
with "n", "%n" would probably have done it too.

Isn't it nice to have so many ways to do the same thing?  And that they're all
so well documented?  ;-)

